# Plan Mode: Front-End UI Enhancement Template

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file provides a specialized planning template for UI/UX enhancements in the PolygonExpress project. It is designed for planning UI improvements with a focus on theme integration, component styling, and consistent user experience.

This file complements:
- **front-end-workflow-reference.md**: Core front-end development workflow
- **plan-mode-front-end-basic.md**: Basic planning template
- **component-patterns.md**: Component implementation patterns

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file is a Manual rule type and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in the plan-mode message-command:

```
plan-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/plan-mode/plan-mode-ui-enhancement.mdc
```

## UI Enhancement Template Structure

When this template is applied, the planning folder will be structured as follows:

```
planning/
  ├── requirements.md (UI/UX requirements)
  ├── images/ (Screenshot folder - provided by Tyler)
  │   ├── current-ui.png (Example: Current UI screenshots)
  │   ├── reference-designs.png (Example: Reference designs from other sites)
  │   └── mockups.png (Example: Design mockups or wireframes)
  ├── context-ui-analysis.md (Existing UI analysis)
  ├── context-theme-integration.md (Theme system analysis)
  ├── context-component-styling.md (Component styling analysis)
  ├── implementation-ui-enhancement.md (UI implementation approach)
  ├── implementation-responsive-design.md (Responsive implementation details)
  ├── test-cheatsheet.md (Visual testing scenarios)
  └── README.md (Overview)
```

## Special Image-Based Planning Process

This UI enhancement planning mode is specialized for visual analysis and design implementation. Tyler Youk will start the process by:

1. Creating and populating the initial `requirements.md` file with specific UI/UX objectives
2. Providing screenshots and reference images in the `images/` folder (or a subfolder structure of his preference)
3. Describing what each image represents in the `requirements.md` file

The images will typically include:
- Screenshots of the current locally hosted front-end application UI
- Reference designs from other websites that should be emulated
- Design mockups or wireframes for the enhanced UI
- UI component examples that showcase desired styling

Using these visual references, you will be able to conduct a more accurate analysis of:
- Current UI structure and styling
- Design patterns and components
- Color schemes and typography
- Layout and responsive design patterns
- Interactive element styling (buttons, forms, etc.)
- Visual consistency across the application

This image-based approach enables more precise planning and implementation of UI enhancements by providing concrete visual context beyond text descriptions alone.

